- Women tend to take on more responsibilities outside of paid labour (such as caregiving) compared to men; 
- Men and women may specialize in different kinds of jobs (men may be overrepresented in higher paying, more skilled roles);
- Men are likely to negotiate higher salaries more than women;
- Employers may hold female employees to higher criteria when evaluating their performance (e.g. expecting better attendance, appearance);
- Gender-based discrimination can influence recruiters and hiring managers when it comes to job offers.

